{"book":7,"chapter":8,"context":{"chapter":8,"title":"Gideon's Victory, Gideon's Snare","summary":"Gideon calms Ephraim, punishes towns that refused his men bread, and executes the Midianite kings. He refuses to be king, but makes a gold ephod that Israel worships, and after his death Israel turns back to Baal.","background":"Zebah and Zalmunna had killed Gideon's brothers at Tabor (vv. 18–19), so their execution was also blood vengeance. The gold Gideon collected weighed 1,700 shekels (v. 26), about 40 pounds. His son by a concubine in Shechem was named Abimelech, 'my father is king' (v. 31), an odd name for the son of a man who refused the crown.","customs":[{"term":"Ephod","verses":"8:27","note":"Usually a priestly garment or object used to seek God's guidance. Gideon's gold ephod became an object of worship and 'a snare' to his family."},{"term":"Ornaments on camels' necks","verses":"8:21-26","note":"The Hebrew word suggests crescent-shaped ornaments, decorations that marked the wealth of the Midianite kings."}],"watchFor":["A soft answer calms Ephraim (vv. 1–3).","'The Lord shall rule over you' (v. 23), followed at once by the ephod (vv. 24–27)."],"connections":["Proverbs 15:1","Exodus 28:6","1 Samuel 8:7","Judges 9:1-6"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיֹּאמְרוּ","vaiyomeru","H559","Hc/Vqw3mp","and they said"],["אֵלָיו","'elav","H413","HRd/Sp3ms","to him"],["אִישׁ","'ish","H376","HNcmsc","[the] man of"],["אֶפְרַיִם","'efrayim","H669","HNpm","Ephraim"],["מָה","mah-","H4100","HPi","what?"],["הַדָּבָר","hadavar","H1697","HTd/Ncmsa","[is] the thing"],["הַזֶּה","hazeh","H2088","HTd/Tm","<the> this"],["עָשִׂיתָ","'asita","H6213","HVqp2ms","[which] you have done"],["לָּנוּ","lanu","H9035","HRd/Sp1bp","to <the> us"],["לְבִלְתִּי","levilti","H1115","HR/Ncbsa","to not"],["קְרֹאות","kerot","H7121","HVqcc","to summon"],["לָנוּ","lanu","H9035","HRd/Sp1bp","<to> <the> us"],["כִּי","ki","H3588","HTc","that"],["הָלַכְתָּ","halakhta","H1980","HVqp2ms","you went"],["לְהִלָּחֵם","lehil