e sister of Gilead. He was the grandson of Manasseh (1 Chr. 7:18). From his family Gideon sprang (Josh. 17:2; comp. Judg. 6:34; 8:2).","verses":4,"father":"Gilead","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"midian_2075","name":"Midian","also":"Midianites, Midianitish","summary":"Strife, the fourth son of Abraham by Keturah, the father of the Midianites (Gen. 25:2; 1 Chr. 1:32).","verses":38,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Keturah","v":[3,5,12,22,26,28]},{"id":"oreb_2255","name":"Oreb","also":"","summary":"Raven, a prince of Midian, who, being defeated by Gideon and put to straits, was slain along with Zeeb (Judg. 7:20-25).","verses":4,"father":"","mother":"","v":[3]},{"id":"zeeb_3033","name":"Zeeb","also":"","summary":"The wolf, one of the two leaders of the great Midianite host which invaded Israel and was utterly routed by Gideon.","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[3]},{"id":"gideon_1314","name":"Gideon","also":"Jerubbaal, Gedeon","summary":"Called also Jerubbaal (Judg. 6:29, 32), was the first of the judges whose history is circumstantially narrated (Judg. 6-8). His calling is the commencement of the second period in the history of the judges.","verses":49,"father":"Joash","mother":"","v":[4,7,11,13,21,22,23,24,27,28,29,30,32,33,35]},{"id":"zalmunna_2983","name":"Zalmunna","also":"","summary":"One of the two kings of Midian whom the “Lord delivered” into the hands of Gideon.","verses":9,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5,6,7,10,12,15,18,21]},{"id":"zebah_2997","name":"Zebah","also":"","summary":"Man-killer, or sacrifice, one of the two kings who led the vast host of the Midianites who invaded the land of Israel, and over whom Gideon gained a great and decisive victory (Judg. 8).","verses":9,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5,6,7,10,12,15,18,21]},{"id":"joash_1630","name":"Joash","also":"","summary":"A contracted form of Jehoash, the father of Gideon (Judg. 6:11, 29; 8:13, 29, 32).","verses":8,"father":"","mother":"","v":[13,29,32]},{"id":"jether_906","name":"Jether","also":"","summary":"The oldest of Gideon’s seventy sons (Judg. 8:20).","verses":1,"father":"Gideon","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[28,33,34]},{"id":"abimelech_41","name":"Abimelech","also":"","summary":"A son of Gideon (Judg. 9:1), who was proclaimed king after the death of his father (Judg. 8:33-9:6). One of his first acts was to murder his brothers, seventy in number, “on one stone,” at Ophrah.","verses":36,"father":"Gideon","mother":"","v":[31]}],"places":[{"id":"midian_796","name":"Midian","kind":"Region","lat":28.75,"lon":34.75,"summary":"An Arabian tribe descended from Midian. They inhabited principally the desert north of the peninsula of Arabia. The peninsula of Sinai was the pasture-ground for their flocks.","verses":44,"v":[1,3,5,12,22,26,28]},{"id":"abiezer_11","name":"Abiezer","kind":"","lat":32.60868,"lon":35.28826,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[2]},{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these two historical fountains there is a third, called the Hasbany, which rises in the bottom of a valley at the western base of Hermon, 12 miles north of Tell-el-Kady.","verses":177,"v":[4]},{"id":"succoth_1113","name":"Succoth","kind":"City","lat":32.19571,"lon":35.62161,"summary":"A city on the east of Jordan, identified with Tell Dar’ala, a high mound, a mass of debris, in the plain north of Jabbok and about one mile from it (Josh. 13:27).","verses":10,"v":[5,6,8,14,15,16]},{"id":"penuel_931","name":"Penuel","kind":"City","lat":32.18437,"lon":35.70287,"summary":"Face of God, a place not far from Succoth, on the east of the Jordan and north of the river Jabbok. It is also called “Peniel.” Here Jacob wrestled (Gen. 32:24-32) “with a man” (“the angel”, Hos. 12:4.","verses":5,"v":[8,9,17]},{"id":"east_348","name":"East","kind":"","lat":31.95019,"lon":35.92413,"summary":"The Arabs as a whole, known as the Nabateans or Kedarenes, nomad tribes (Judg. 6:3, 33; 7:12; 8:10).","verses":6,"v":[10]},{"id":"karkor_669","name":"Karkor","kind":"","lat":32.18437,"lon":35.70287,"summary":"Foundation, a place in the open desert wastes on the east of Jordan (Judg. 8:10), not far beyond Succoth and Penuel, to the south.","verses":1,"v":[10]},{"id":"jogbehah_645","name":"Jogbehah","kind":"","lat":32.02874,"lon":35.86289,"summary":"","verses":2,"v":[11]},{"id":"nobah_901","name":"Nobah","kind":"","lat":32.75692,"lon":36.6164,"summary":"The name given to Kenath by Nobah when he conquered it.","verses":2,"v":[11]},{"id":"heres_562","name":"Heres","kind":"","lat":32.19998,"lon":35.63331,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[13]},{"id":"tabor_1128","name":"Tabor","kind":"Mountain","lat":32.68711,"lon":35.39038,"summary":"Now Jebel et-Tur, a cone-like prominent mountain, 11 miles west of the Sea of Galilee. It is about 1,843 feet high. The view from the summit of it is said to be singularly extensive and grand.","verses":5,"v":[18]},{"id":"ophrah_914","name":"Ophrah","kind":"City","lat":32.60868,"lon":35.28826,"summary":"“Of the Abi-ezrites.” A city of Manasseh, 6 miles south-west of Shechem, the residence of Gideon (Judg. 6:11; 8:27, 32). After his great victory over the Midianites, he slew at this place the captive kings (8:18-21).","verses":5,"v":[27,32]},{"id":"shechem_1069","name":"Shechem","kind":"City","lat":32.22111,"lon":35.25444,"summary":"A city in Samaria (Gen. 33:18), called also Sichem (12:6), Sychem (Acts 7:16). It stood in the narrow sheltered valley between Ebal on the north and Gerizim on the south, these mountains at their base being only some 500 yards apart.","verses":40,"v":[31]}],"events":[{"id":"deliverance_by_gideon_141","title":"Deliv